[Term]
id: UBERON:0000307
name: blastula
namespace: uberon
alt_id: UBERON:0007011
def: "Organism at the blastula stage - an early stage of embryonic development in animals. It is produced by cleavage of a fertilized ovum and consists of a spherical layer of around 128 cells surrounding a central fluid-filled cavity called the blastocoel. The blastula follows the morula and precedes the gastrula in the developmental sequence." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blastula]
