[Term]
id: UBERON:0002514
name: intramembranous bone
namespace: uberon
def: "Bone tissue forms directly within mesenchyme, and does not replace other tissues[TAO]. Intramembranous ossification is the formation of bone in which osteoblasts secrete a collagen-proteoglycan matrix that binds calcium salts and becomes calcified[GO]. Intramembranous ossification is the way flat bones and the shell of a turtle are formed[GO]. Unlike endochondral ossification, cartilage is not present during intramembranous ossification[WP]." [GO:0001957, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intramembranous_ossification, https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/267]
synonym: "intramembranous bones" RELATED PLURAL [ZFA:0001635]
synonym: "membrane bone" RELATED [AEO:0000085]
