[Term]
id: UBERON:0010428
name: flat bone
namespace: uberon
def: "A bone that is shaped as a broad flat plate and composed of two thin layers of compact tissue enclosing between them a variable quantity of cancellous tissue, which is the location of red bone marrow." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flat_bone]
comment: Examples: cranium, the ilium, sternum, rib cage, the sacrum and the scapula; the occipital, parietal, frontal, nasal, lacrimal, vomer, scapula, os coxC&, sternum, and ribs
