property_value: UBPROP:0000003 "The central cavity within the mesoderm is the paired primary or embryonic coelom. Parts of the embryonic coelom often become enclosed in the mesoderm, forming a myocoel within the epimere, a nephrocoel within the mesomere, and simple coelom (body cavity) within the lateral plate mesoderm.[well established][VHOG]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-17", external_class="VHOG:0001283", ontology="VHOG", source="http://bgee.unil.ch/", source="ISBN:978-0072528305 Kardong KV, Vertebrates: Comparative Anatomy, Function, Evolution (2006) p.166 and Figure 5.6"}

